# Git and automatic commits

- Commit each completed, verified task slice automatically, including documentation and rule-only changes. Do not wait for a separate commit request.
- Before editing, note `HEAD` and working-tree status. Do not stage or commit unrelated or pre-existing user changes.
- Never use `git add .`, `git add -A`, or `git commit -a`; stage explicit task paths only. Stop and report a staged-file conflict before committing.
- Write commit messages in English following standard Conventional Commits.
- Do not push, amend, or rewrite history unless the user explicitly asks.
